              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "Base: the last 12 months of actuals, scaled to a full year. Utilisation scales the team's hours; rates and realisation scale the fee on each hour. Hires bill at the firm's utilisation × year-one productivity (or the chosen area's rate and workload). People leaving: pay saved, fees lost except the share the team keeps; NES redundancy (s 119) and notice (s 117) are paid once. A branch ramps up in a straight line; fit-out is cash, not profit. Marketing buys inquiries at 40% of the channel's current cost with diminishing returns, billing 35% of a typical matter in year one, up to 95% utilisation. A new matter type ramps to its mature volume; the launch campaign is one-off cash. Cash: one-off costs are paid in week one of the 13-week forecast. Sample data. A decision aid, not legal or financial advice.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "8pt",
                      "color": "#64748b",
